Subject: [PATCH] v8 turboshaft: avoid explicit-template Tuple<> for GCC 16

GCC 16 rejects '__ Tuple<Word32, Word32>(result, ...)' when result is
a ScopedVar<Word32>; it parses the expression as a function-style
cast to Tuple<Word32, Word32> rather than a constructor call and
bails with 'instantiating erroneous template'. The other call sites
use CTAD (no explicit args), which works.

Rewrite the two offending calls with a temporary V<Word32> so CTAD
can deduce Tuple<Word32, Word32> like elsewhere in the file.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/deps/v8/src/compiler/turboshaft/int64-lowering-reducer.h
+++ b/deps/v8/src/compiler/turboshaft/int64-lowering-reducer.h
@@ -637,7 +637,8 @@
       result = __ Word32CountLeadingZeros(high);
     }
 
-    return __ Tuple<Word32, Word32>(result, __ Word32Constant(0));
+    V<Word32> low_part = result;
+    return __ Tuple(low_part, __ Word32Constant(0));
   }
 
   V<Word32Pair> LowerCtz(V<Word32Pair> input) {
@@ -650,7 +651,8 @@
       result = __ Word32CountTrailingZeros(low);
     }
 
-    return __ Tuple<Word32, Word32>(result, __ Word32Constant(0));
+    V<Word32> low_part = result;
+    return __ Tuple(low_part, __ Word32Constant(0));
   }
 
   V<Word32Pair> LowerPopCount(V<Word32Pair> input) {
